    "Concepts to know in git\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Clone - allows y ou to copy an entire codebase \n",
    "2. commit -  commit is a permanent save point (snapshot) of your project's  files at a specific moment in time, stored safely in your local repository's history\n",
    "3. Push - Uploads your saved changes from your computer to GitHub so others can see them.\n",
    "4. Pull - Downloads new updates from GitHub and immediately blends them into your active files \n",
    "5. Staging -  A \"waiting room\" where you pick which modified files you want to include in your next save point"
    "5. Staging -  A \"waiting room\" where you pick which modified files you want to include in your next save point\n",
    "6. Branch-  A separate, parallel timeline of your project. You create a branch to build a new feature safely without touching the main code\n",
    "7. Merge -   Combining the changes from one branch (like your new feature) back into another branch (like main)\n",
